* signal generated using 2 methods

	1. Other processes 	2. Hardware (eg : ^C)

Other process or Hardware not send directly, send via signal manager.

* Life of the signal start when somebody generate the signal. 

* Life of the signal ends when signal manager deliver the signal to the particular process.



kill
----

#include <sys/types.h>
#include <signal.h>

int kill(pid_t pid, int sig);

if atleast one signal send successfully it returns 0. On failure returns -1.


raise
-----

raise send a signal to the caller.

int raise(int signal);

return 0 on sucess. non zero on failure.


pause
-----

int pause(void);

pause() causes the calling process or thread to sleep until a signal is delivered that either terminates the process or causes the invocation of a signal catching information.



























